# Header: Apple's virtiofs server answers each new name with a LOOKUP
# (ENOENT, no negative timeout). During npm install about half of all
# LOOKUPs probe names in directories this guest has just made. A
# directory made here with MKDIR starts empty, and the Mac's changes
# under bind sources reach the guest through /proc/ctrs/fsnotify (patch
# 0006). For ten seconds after MKDIR, a lookup of a name missing from
# the dcache in such a directory answers ENOENT without a request, and
# its positive children are kept in the dcache. The directory loses the
# status when a positive child is pruned or fails revalidation, when a
# create races to EEXIST, or when a Mac-side event names it or one of
# its missing descendants.
